<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Child car seats can be carried on-board most Qantas and QantasLink flights and secured to an aircraft seat if approved by Qantas prior to travel.<br />
<br />
Please ensure you first read the relevant information, including the certifications and guides on child car seats and restraints.<br />
<br />
To obtain pre-approval of your child’s car seat, please complete the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs.html">Accessibility, Medical and Inclusive Requests</a> and provide the below information:
<ul>
	<li>Make/Model of car seat&nbsp;</li>
	<li>Manufacturing country&nbsp;</li>
	<li>Rear or Forward Facing&nbsp;</li>
	<li>An aircraft approved sticker must be attached to the car seat</li>
</ul>
Final approval is given by Airport staff upon sighting the car seat.<br />
<br />
While we make every effort to carry passengers in pre-assigned seating, seating is subject to change for operational, safety or security reasons, even after boarding.<br />
<br />
If any of your flights are operated by an airline other than Qantas, you must obtain approval for the car seat or child restraint system from that airline.<br />
&nbsp;</body>
</html>